WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.948 --> 00:00:03.531
(gentle music)

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.963
- The Bachelorette, the entire process.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.410
I was talking about it
for a couple of weeks,

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:14.540
but when I knew that I finally was ready

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:15.770
and that I wanted to do this again,

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:17.163
there was no turning back.

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:19.977
(gentle music)

00:00:19.977 --> 00:00:23.170
Oh yeah I have grown a lot.

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:26.203
I have become much more
patient I would say.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.930
And I feel like, especially
this time around,

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:30.680
I have become much more confident

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.850
and just really comfortable in my own skin

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:33.913
and with who I am.

00:00:34.313 --> 00:00:36.896
(gentle music)

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.790
No so actually how it all worked out is

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:42.000
I knew that it would be Arie

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.550
because he was announced I
think on Good Morning America

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.460
and then that day that he was announced,

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:49.400
I got the final call saying we want you.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.330
Come out to California.

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:52.440
So I knew at that point
it was going to be Arie

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:53.273
and not Peter.

00:00:53.555 --> 00:00:56.138
(gentle music)

00:00:56.243 --> 00:01:00.820
Oh my god I ate so much every night.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:02.930
The entire night for
the guys in the kitchen

00:01:03.206 --> 00:01:04.660
they have a caterer so
they have everything

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.483
from little Hors d'oeuvre to
mac and cheese to chicken.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:12.400
But I don't get to go into
the kitchen unfortunately

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.950
so I would just have a
ton of chicken nuggets

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.593
and a ton of peanut butter.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:20.080
That's what got me
through the entire season.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.570
Filming, you know, we started,
I probably go to the mansion

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:25.060
around 7:30 I would say

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.170
and I probably walked out the next morning

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:29.100
at around 8:30 or 9:00.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.750
But I have a lot of snack breaks.

00:01:31.266 --> 00:01:32.099
(laughing)

00:01:32.099 --> 00:01:34.682
(gentle music)

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:37.520
Okay so we do get a packing list.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.766
It is very generic so
it's like some jeans,

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:43.027
some sweaters, some
shorts, a couple dresses.

00:01:43.027 --> 00:01:46.990
But we have to pack everything
into only two suit cases

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:48.620
and you're potentially gone for two months

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.140
and so it's difficult.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:52.820
I am the worst packer in the entire world

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:55.972
and I over pack and so
I had a lot of stuff.

00:01:55.972 --> 00:01:58.555
(gentle music)

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:03.313
I do still have all of
the dresses from Rachel.

00:02:03.458 --> 00:02:04.853
Actually not all of them.

00:02:05.586 --> 00:02:06.840
I got I think five or six of them

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:10.080
and then the jewelry I
got one pair of earrings

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:11.690
from Neil Lane that I got to keep.

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:13.193
So yes I do still have it all.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:14.253
Oh and the shoes.

00:02:14.962 --> 00:02:15.795
(laughing)

00:02:15.795 --> 00:02:17.633
I got the beautiful silver shoes too,

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.210
which actually weirdly enough
I'll still put on sometimes

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:21.960
at my apartment and walk around in.

00:02:22.114 --> 00:02:24.697
(gentle music)

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:27.153
Oh god.

00:02:27.153 --> 00:02:28.530
So when my ex showed up in Peru,

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:31.768
that was probably the biggest blindside

00:02:31.768 --> 00:02:34.380
I had had up until the breakup.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.280
I did not see it coming.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.480
I honestly thought when I
heard the knock on the door

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:40.170
that it would be either
one of the producers

00:02:40.211 --> 00:02:42.993
or Arie himself just coming over.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:46.343
I did not expect to see
Ross on the other end.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.297
It wasn't a pleasant surprise though.

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:51.243
- No not at all.

00:02:51.243 --> 00:02:53.000
I have not talked to him since then.

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:55.224
He shouldn't have even
came if I'm being honest.

00:02:55.224 --> 00:02:57.807
(gentle music)

00:02:59.313 --> 00:03:01.340
I mean last season and this
season it's always a change

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:04.740
when you realize how exhausting it is

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.270
and you don't get a ton of sleep.

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:07.660
One of the best surprises though

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:10.430
is I think just meeting
all the girls last year

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:13.500
and really becoming close
friends with a lot of them

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.250
and not only building the friendship,

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.410
but knowing that those friendships

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:17.860
are going to last a lifetime.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:20.823
(gentle music)

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:26.100
The girls okay well so we're
filming most of the time.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.420
I've never lived in a sorority,

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.830
but I can only imagine that's
kind of what it's like.

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:31.680
You're just cooking meals together

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:32.930
and you're drinking coffee together

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:34.250
and you're laying by the pool

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:35.630
and you don't have your phone.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:36.463
You don't have a TV.

00:03:36.463 --> 00:03:37.460
You don't have music

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:38.866
and so it's really just interacting

00:03:38.866 --> 00:03:40.700
and building friendships with these women

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:44.410
and, especially last season,
we I think were really lucky

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:46.760
with the group of girls
that were all together.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:49.673
(gentle music)

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:53.030
One of them I will say
it's not my best moment,

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:55.440
but I had a few cocktails
and I took a long nap

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.493
behind a couch for a while
on one of the group dates.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:01.923
- Behind a couch.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:04.663
It was behind a couch and a fireplace.

00:04:04.772 --> 00:04:07.763
I was just sitting there and
talking with, I think Chelsea,

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:12.163
and it was just so cozy I
just drifted off to sleep.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:15.303
She's a mom so she got a
pillow, put it under my head,

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:17.390
covered me with a nice fur blanket.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.776
I'm actually kind of
glad that didn't make TV.

00:04:19.776 --> 00:04:22.359
(gentle music)

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:28.460
Quite honestly everyone was portrayed

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:30.770
as how they were in the moment

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:34.167
and how things were playing
along during that day

00:04:34.167 --> 00:04:35.340
or that week.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:37.850
You know there was drama with Krystal

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:39.150
between some of the girls,

00:04:39.763 --> 00:04:41.770
but Krystal is a good person.

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:43.920
She was kind, she got
along well with the girls

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:46.530
for the most part, but there
were moments with people,

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:48.640
you know, kind of get a little stir crazy

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:49.490
and things happen,

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:54.010
but everything we all say and
do is real and it's organic

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:57.363
and so I think that was all
captured as it really happened.

00:04:57.732 --> 00:05:00.180
(gentle music)

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:03.000
No I didn't think that Arie

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.920
was going to end the engagement.

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:06.380
I knew that he had been struggling

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:09.270
with his feelings and feeling guilty

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:11.090
in how he sent Lauren home,

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:16.090
but I didn't see the break
up that day happening at all.

00:05:16.293 --> 00:05:18.876
(gentle music)

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:23.010
I still keep in touch
with a lot of the girls

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.713
actually from Arie's season.

00:05:24.868 --> 00:05:28.490
Yeah a lot of the girls, I
mean, and you'll see them

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:30.970
throughout the girls that
were on After the Final Rose

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:34.820
with me have stuck by my side
throughout the entire journey,

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:36.820
but I'll still talk to Chelsea.

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:38.470
I'll still talk to Ashley.

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:39.828
Some of the other girls too.

00:05:39.828 --> 00:05:42.411
(gentle music)

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:46.520
Oh man see this is the
thing it's hard with advice

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:48.120
because everyone is so different,

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:51.830
but for me when I went through
the break up with Arie,

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:55.630
I wanted to just go back to my normal life

00:05:56.505 --> 00:05:58.760
and just still do me and so I
went straight back into work

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:02.840
and I stayed busy and I was
with my friends and family

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:05.790
and I think staying
busy and still doing me

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:07.620
and doing my normal routine helped,

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:12.260
but then also I journal
a ton so that helped me

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:15.880
really sift through my
thoughts, my feelings,

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:17.580
where I was at day by day

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:19.680
and then, I mean, I don't know

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:21.440
this girl can do this,

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:25.020
but it helped watching
my season back with Arie

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:27.820
and watching his relationship with Lauren

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:28.980
and the other women unfold.

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:32.800
To kind of see where he was
in his relationship with me

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:33.863
versus the others.

00:06:34.128 --> 00:06:36.711
(gentle music)

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:40.640
No I honestly I don't think
I would change anything.

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:43.190
I don't really regret anything.

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:45.010
I feel like I really
stayed true to who I was

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:46.280
and said what I wanted to say,

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:48.932
did what I wanted or had
to do in each moment.

00:06:48.932 --> 00:06:51.425
Yeah I think, I mean,

00:06:51.425 --> 00:06:53.713
no I don't think I would change anything.

00:06:53.749 --> 00:06:56.332
(gentle music)

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:03.340
I am open to doing whatever
is best for my relationship

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:04.543
and with my partner.

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:06.740
And as much as I love Minnesota,

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:09.830
I don't feel like I need
to always stay there

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:12.289
and so it's really what
my partner and I decide,

00:07:12.289 --> 00:07:15.730
whether if we end up in
LA or a different city

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:17.780
that neither of us have lived in before.

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:18.910
I'm cool with that too.

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:20.023
I'm open to anything.

00:07:20.401 --> 00:07:22.984
(gentle music)

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.390
Future advice to any
bachelor bachelorettes

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:28.900
would be always carry a snack on you

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:30.500
because the days are long

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:33.300
and you never know when you're
going to have a proper meal.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.390
Mine was peanut butter.

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:36.140
I always kept peanut butter on me.

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:38.419
And just make sure you
take time for yourself.

00:07:38.419 --> 00:07:41.960
Whether it's to journal
or just sit and think

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:45.213
or just stand in your shower
for an 10 or 15 minutes.

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.510
You'll that alone time

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:50.170
because you're constantly
around people 24/7.

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:51.590
So take time for yourself.

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:52.740
Take care of your body.

00:07:53.187 --> 00:07:55.013
Listen to yourself when
you need it the most.

00:07:55.779 --> 00:07:58.362
(gentle music)

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:01.230
I 1000% believe in the journey.

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:02.810
It worked last time around

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:05.107
and worked this time around.

00:08:05.107 --> 00:08:06.470
So much more.

00:08:06.470 --> 00:08:09.290
And yeah it works, it works.

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:12.340
It's a crazy, unconventional
worthwhile journey

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:13.580
but you can find love.

00:08:25.054 --> 00:08:27.033
(whooshing)

